# The `web` service builds the Next.js app and nothing else. `cli/` is a
# separate npm package with its own dependencies and its own release; uploading
# it would only make every deploy slower.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. These are gitignore-style patterns, so a
# bare `cli/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth — which silently
# swallowed `src/app/api/cli/` and shipped a build with no sign-in route.
/cli/
